<p class="wp-block-paragraph">An automatic time log saves you from trying to reconstruct your week on Friday afternoon. But there can still be a pile of unassigned work to sort into projects. Timing&#8217;s new MCP server gives your AI agent a way to help with that part.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Timing records which apps, documents, and websites you use on your Mac. You don&#8217;t have to remember to start a timer when you switch jobs. Its rules can categorize that activity as you work.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The new connection lets an agent such as Claude Code or Codex work with that record. MCP is the protocol that connects the agent to Timing, so you can ask questions about your time and have it help organize the results.</p>



